---
// Whereabouts landing page. Deliberately plain: a confident README, not a
// designed "landing experience". System fonts, zero third-party requests.
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<title>Whereabouts — self-hosted family location sharing</title>
		<meta
			name="description"
			content="A self-hostable fork of Paralino. End-to-end encrypted family location sharing on your own server. No Google, no subscriptions."
		/>
		<meta property="og:title" content="Whereabouts" />
		<meta
			property="og:description"
			content="Self-hosted, end-to-end encrypted family location sharing. Your server, your data."
		/>
		<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
	</head>
	<body>
		<main>
			<h1>Whereabouts</h1>
			<p class="tagline">
				A self-hostable fork of <a href="https://github.com/paralino/paralino">Paralino</a>, the end-to-end encrypted
				family location app. The backend runs on your server. No Google, no subscriptions.
			</p>

			<figure>
				<img src="/screenshot.webp" alt="Whereabouts map screen showing a shared group, member locations, and the Members and Places tabs." width="340" loading="eager" />
				<figcaption>T4Group on the dev build, MapTiler satellite-off, places list empty.</figcaption>
			</figure>

			<h2 id="install">Install</h2>
			<p>
				Download <a href="https://github.com/blazebsc/whereabouts/releases/latest">the latest APK</a> and install it (Android
				will ask you to allow unknown apps once). The app asks for your server URL on first launch; point it at your
				backend and it configures itself.
			</p>
			<p>
				Updates are checked against this repo's releases: Settings, Info &amp; support, <em>Check for updates</em>. No
				store, no account.
			</p>

			<h2 id="self-host">Self-hosting</h2>
			<p>Five steps, roughly twenty minutes on a box with Docker:</p>
			<ol>
				<li>Install <a href="https://appwrite.io/docs/installation">Appwrite</a>, or use their cloud</li>
				<li>Create a project, register an Android platform with the package id <code>app.whereabouts.android</code></li>
				<li>Run <code>backend/provision/provision.mjs</code> to create the schema</li>
				<li>Deploy <code>backend/functions/api</code> as a Node function</li>
				<li>Install the APK and enter the function's URL at setup</li>
			</ol>
			<p>
				The full walkthrough is in <a href="https://github.com/blazebsc/whereabouts/blob/main/SELF_HOSTING.md">SELF_HOSTING.md</a>,
				including the optional <code>MAPTILER_TOKEN</code> variable that unlocks MapTiler styles on every connected device.
			</p>

			<h2 id="changes">What changed from upstream</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Billing is gone. Every feature the plans used to gate is free, the billing routes return 501.</li>
				<li>
					Push is de-Googled: UnifiedPush with RFC 8291 WebPush encryption, tested against{" "}
					<a href="https://ntfy.sh">ntfy</a> and Sunup, with a WebSocket fallback for devices without a distributor.
				</li>
				<li>The server URL is a first-launch setting, not a compile-time constant.</li>
				<li>MapTiler "premium" maps are unlocked by a server env var instead of a subscription.</li>
				<li>Rename to Whereabouts (package <code>app.whereabouts.android</code>, iOS <code>app.whereabouts.ios</code>).</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 id="privacy">What the server can't see</h2>
			<p>
				Locations, places, messages and keys are encrypted on the device before upload. The server stores ciphertext and
				passes it along; it holds no key. What it can see: that accounts and groups exist, row sizes, timestamps, and the
				push endpoints devices register. Group keys move through a pre-key handshake, same as upstream.
			</p>

			<h2 id="status">Status</h2>
			<p>
				Android builds are signed and published on the releases page. iOS has been renamed but is otherwise untouched
				upstream code. Both app builds are covered by CI on every push.
			</p>
		</main>

		<footer>
			<p>
				AGPL-3.0. Not affiliated with Paralino; if you'd rather have the hosted original, use{" "}
				<a href="https://github.com/paralino/paralino">theirs</a> (it's great software).
			</p>
			<p>
				<a href="https://github.com/blazebsc/whereabouts">Source</a> ·
				<a href="https://github.com/blazebsc/whereabouts/releases">Releases</a> ·
				<a href="https://github.com/blazebsc/whereabouts/blob/main/SELF_HOSTING.md">Self-hosting guide</a>
			</p>
		</footer>
	</body>
</html>

<style is:global>
	:root {
		--text: #1a1a1a;
		--muted: #555;
		--link: #0057c2;
		--rule: #ddd;
		--code-bg: #f2f2f0;
	}

	* {
		box-sizing: border-box;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
	}

	body {
		font-family:
			system-ui,
			-apple-system,
			"Segoe UI",
			Roboto,
			sans-serif;
		font-size: 16.5px;
		line-height: 1.65;
		color: var(--text);
		background: #fff;
	}

	main {
		max-width: 680px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 48px 22px 24px;
	}

	h1 {
		font-size: 2rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
	}

	.tagline {
		font-size: 1.12rem;
		color: var(--muted);
		margin-top: 8px;
	}

	figure {
		margin: 28px auto;
		width: fit-content;
		text-align: center;
	}
	figure img {
		width: 340px;
		max-width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		border-radius: 10px;
	}
	figcaption {
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: var(--muted);
		margin-top: 8px;
	}

	h2 {
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		font-weight: 650;
		margin: 36px 0 10px;
		padding-top: 22px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	p,
	ol,
	ul {
		margin: 10px 0;
	}
	li {
		margin: 6px 0 6px 22px;
	}

	a {
		color: var(--link);
		text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
		text-underline-offset: 2px;
	}
	a:hover {
		text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
	}

	code {
		font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", "Cascadia Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
		font-size: 0.86em;
		background: var(--code-bg);
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		border-radius: 4px;
		padding: 1px 5px;
	}

	footer {
		max-width: 680px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 20px 22px 56px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
		font-size: 0.92rem;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	footer p + p {
		margin-top: 6px;
	}
</style>
